Foldpeak - Privacy Policy

Last updated: 21 November 2026

Foldpeak is a mobile solitaire card game made by CodingTech Studio, Başakşehir / İstanbul, Türkiye ("we").
Contact: codingtechstudio@gmail.com

Foldpeak is made for adults. It is not directed to children and we do not knowingly collect data from children.


1. What stays on your device

Your progress, coins, wild cards, folded figures, achievements, daily hand streak and settings are stored only on your device. We have no account system and no server of our own, and the game sends no play statistics or crash reports. Deleting the game deletes this data.


2. Ads

The game shows ads through Google AdMob: videos you choose to watch for a reward (a wild card, five extra cards, double coins or keeping your daily streak), full-screen ads between some hands, and a banner at the bottom of the hand screen. To show and measure ads, Google receives the advertising identifier of your device, your IP address (from which an approximate location is derived), device information and your interactions with the ads.

In the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland, a consent form from Google asks for your choice before any ad is requested. Elsewhere the game asks with its own window ("Allow" / "Don't allow"). Without your consent to personalised ads, only non-personalised ads are requested. You can reopen your choice at any time under Settings > Privacy > Options. You can also reset or delete the advertising identifier in your device settings.

"Remove ads" in the shop turns off the ads between hands and the banner; videos for rewards stay available if you want them.

How Google uses data from apps that use its services: https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites


3. Purchases

If you buy something in the shop, the payment is handled entirely by Google Play (or the App Store). We never see your card or payment details. The game only learns from the store which product was bought and keeps the transaction identifier on your device so that a product is delivered once. "Restore purchases" in the shop asks the store again which one-time products your store account owns.


4. Who receives data

Google Ireland Limited / Google LLC, as the provider of AdMob and of Google Play billing. Google may process data on servers outside your country, including the United States; it relies on the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework and standard contractual clauses. We do not sell your data and we share it with no one else.


5. How long data is kept

Data on your device: until you delete the game or its data. Ad data is kept by Google under its own policies.


6. Your rights

Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR, the UK GDPR or the Turkish Law No. 6698, KVKK), you have the right to ask what data is held about you, to have it corrected or deleted, to object to or restrict its use, to withdraw your consent at any time, and to complain to your data protection authority. We hold no personal data about you on our side; for ad data you can change your choice in the game and reset your advertising identifier, and you can write to codingtechstudio@gmail.com with any question. We answer within 30 days.


7. Permissions

Internet access and network state (ads, purchases), the advertising identifier (ads), billing (purchases through Google Play) and vibration (short feedback pulses you can switch off in Settings).


8. Changes

If this policy changes, the date at the top changes and the new text is published at the same address.


